## Examples

**Read with Ctrl+Shift+Space instead of Ctrl+Alt+R** (change line `Id = 1`):

```csharp
new Shortcut { Id = 1, Mods = MOD_CONTROL | MOD_SHIFT, Key = Keys.Space,  Label = "Read highlighted text / Stop", Run = ReadOrStop },
```

**Read with just the Pause/Break key:**

```csharp
new Shortcut { Id = 1, Mods = 0, Key = Keys.Pause,  Label = "Read highlighted text / Stop", Run = ReadOrStop },
```

**Pause with Ctrl+Alt+Space instead of Ctrl+Alt+P** (change line `Id = 2`):

```csharp
new Shortcut { Id = 2, Mods = MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT, Key = Keys.Space,  Label = "Pause / Resume", Run = () => synth.PauseOrResume() },
```

**Faster and slower on the arrow keys** (lines `Id = 3` and `Id = 4`):

```csharp
new Shortcut { Id = 3, Mods = MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT, Key = Keys.Up,    Label = "Speak faster", Run = () => ChangeRate(+1) },
new Shortcut { Id = 4, Mods = MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT, Key = Keys.Down,  Label = "Speak slower", Run = () => ChangeRate(-1) },
```

The tray menu and pop-ups update automatically to show your new keys.

