## Changing the "Change read shortcut" menu list

The choices in the tray's **Change read shortcut** menu come from two lines just above the shortcuts block. Search for `ReadMods`:

```csharp
static readonly uint[] ReadMods = { MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT, MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT, MOD_CONTROL | MOD_SHIFT, MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT, 0 };
static readonly Keys[] ReadKeys = { Keys.R, Keys.Space, Keys.Space, Keys.F12, Keys.Pause };
```

These two lists work as pairs, read left to right. The 1st modifier goes with the 1st key, the 2nd with the 2nd, and so on. The default pairs are:

| # | Modifier | Key | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `MOD_CONTROL \| MOD_ALT` | `Keys.R` | Ctrl+Alt+R |
| 2 | `MOD_CONTROL \| MOD_ALT` | `Keys.Space` | Ctrl+Alt+Space |
| 3 | `MOD_CONTROL \| MOD_SHIFT` | `Keys.Space` | Ctrl+Shift+Space |
| 4 | `MOD_CONTROL \| MOD_ALT` | `Keys.F12` | Ctrl+Alt+F12 |
| 5 | `0` | `Keys.Pause` | Pause/Break |

To add or remove a choice, add or remove an entry **in both lists at the same position**. The two lists must always have the same number of entries.

If the read shortcut is already taken when the app starts, Read Aloud tries these in order and uses the first free one.

