## Troubleshooting

| What you see | What to do |
|---|---|
| "Read Aloud couldn't start" with an error | A typing mistake in `ReadAloud.cs`. The message gives the line number. Check for a missing comma, a missing `\|`, or wrong capital letters in a `Keys.` name. The full error is also saved in `ReadAloud-error.txt`. |
| "These shortcuts are already used by another program" | Another app owns that combination. Choose different keys. |
| My new read shortcut is ignored | The old one is still saved. See [Clear the saved read shortcut](#important-clear-the-saved-read-shortcut). |
| Nothing changed | Make sure you saved the file and fully quit Read Aloud from the tray before starting it again. |
| It all went wrong | Put back your saved copy of `ReadAloud.cs`, or run `Install.cmd` again from the original download. |